{"Concurrent inserts exceed limit: The active-device count and the insert run as separate database operations. A burst of requests with different new device ids can all read count < deviceLimit and then all insert, leaving more active anonymous devices than the configured cap.": 0.93031907081604, "Rejected devices stay cached: When a new device is over the limit, tagDeviceUI has already written its device id into the local cache before the store returns ErrDeviceLimitReached. This branch rejects the first request, but the next request from the same device hits the cache, skips the store check, and authenticates until the cache entry expires.": 0.9656682014465332, "Negative limit disables enforcement: A negative device_limit parses successfully, but the store only enforces the cap when the value is greater than zero. A configuration typo such as device_limit = -1 silently turns the limit off instead of failing startup.": 0.8409415483474731}